  "/fca-licence-car-dealers": {
    "title": "FCA Licence for Car Dealers: Authorisation, FRNs and Permissions",
    "answer": "“FCA licence” is a common way of referring to Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) authorisation. For a car dealer, the important checks are the firm’s regulatory status, its permitted activities and any restrictions. A Firm Reference Number (FRN) identifies a firm; the number alone does not show that it can carry out every type of finance activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "What the terminology means",
        "paragraphs": [],
        "bullets": [],
        "columns": [
          "Term",
          "Meaning for your dealership"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Authorisation",
            "The firm’s authorisation to undertake specified regulated activities, subject to its permissions and requirements."
          ],
          [
            "Permission",
            "The scope of regulated activities the firm may carry out, including applicable limitations."
          ],
          [
            "FRN",
            "The reference used to identify a firm in FCA records. Check the associated entry and current status."
          ],
          [
            "Appointed representative",
            "A firm carrying on agreed activities under a principal’s responsibility; this is different from holding its own direct authorisation."
          ]
        ],
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "apply",
            "label": "FCA: applying for authorisation",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/authorisation/apply"
          },
          {
            "id": "register",
            "label": "FCA: Financial Services Register",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/financial-services-register"
          },
          {
            "id": "small",
            "label": "FCA: regulatory guide for credit brokers",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/regulatory-guide-credit-brokers"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "id": "guide-section-1"
      },
      {
        "title": "How to check a dealership on the Register",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Use the FCA’s official Register and search by the legal name or FRN. Match the entry to the business you are dealing with rather than relying on a copied logo or number.",
          "Check the current status, the relevant permissions and restrictions, and any principal relationship. Read the entry’s details alongside the proposed activity. Use contact details on the official record when checking a mismatch, rather than a number supplied in an unexpected message."
        ],
        "bullets": [
          "Match the legal entity, trading name and contact information.",
          "Check the status is current, not a historical authorisation.",
          "Look for the activity you intend to carry out and any limitations.",
          "For an AR, verify the principal and the scope of the arrangement."
        ],
        "columns": [
          "What you find",
          "Practical next step"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "A current entry matching the legal entity",
            "Check the specific activity and restrictions as well as the name and number."
          ],
          [
            "An appointed representative (AR) entry",
            "Check the named principal and ask it to confirm the activities covered."
          ],
          [
            "A former name, cancelled status or mismatched contact details",
            "Do not rely on the copied number. Check the official record and resolve the mismatch before relying on the status."
          ]
        ],
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "register",
            "label": "FCA: Financial Services Register",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/financial-services-register"
          },
          {
            "id": "check",
            "label": "FCA: checking a firm’s authorisation",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/consumers/how-check-firm-individual-authorised"
          }
        ],
        "links": [
          [
            "/do-motor-dealers-need-fca-authorisation",
            "Check whether your activities need authorisation"
          ]
        ],
        "id": "guide-section-2"
      },
      {
        "title": "An FRN is not an endorsement",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Describe the dealership’s actual status accurately in customer communications. Do not treat authorisation as an FCA recommendation of the business or its products. An application in progress is not the same as approval.",
          "For example, a dealer should not reuse a predecessor company’s regulatory wording just because the trading name and premises look the same. First establish which legal entity will carry on the activity."
        ],
        "bullets": [],
        "columns": [],
        "rows": [],
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "promotions",
            "label": "FCA: key rules for credit brokers",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/credit-broking-rules"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "id": "guide-section-3"
      },
      {
        "title": "If you are applying for the first time",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Start with your business model and required activities, then prepare an application consistent with them. The application, website and customer process should describe the same business.",
          "The FCA assesses the applicant firm. Support with documents does not transfer responsibility for understanding and explaining the application. Separate the FCA application fee from any consultant’s service charge when budgeting; paying for assistance is not an FCA authorisation fee."
        ],
        "bullets": [],
        "columns": [],
        "rows": [],
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "apply",
            "label": "FCA: applying for authorisation",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/authorisation/apply"
          },
          {
            "id": "broker",
            "label": "FCA: applying as a consumer credit broker",
            "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/authorisation/consumer-credit-brokers"
          }
        ],
        "links": [
          [
            "/fca-application-documents-motor-dealers",
            "See the application document checklist"
          ],
          [
            "/why-fca-applications-get-delayed",
            "Understand assessment and clarification requests"
          ]
        ],
        "id": "guide-section-4"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Is an FCA licence the same as an FRN?",
        "answer": "No. An FRN is an identifier. Check the firm’s status, permissions and limitations to understand what it may do."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does authorisation cover all finance products?",
        "answer": "No. The firm must act within the activities and limitations of its permission or the agreed scope of its principal arrangement."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can we describe an application as FCA approval?",
        "answer": "No. Submitting an application does not mean the FCA has authorised the firm."
      }
    ],
    "related": [
      "/do-motor-dealers-need-fca-authorisation",
      "/limited-permission-fca-authorisation-motor-dealers",
      "/website-compliance-motor-dealers"
    ],
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "register",
        "label": "FCA: Financial Services Register",
        "href": "https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/financial-services-register"
      },
      {
        "id": "apply",
