  "/credit-broking-permission-motor-dealers": {
    "title": "Credit Broking Permission for Motor Dealers",
    "answer": "A motor dealer can carry on credit broking by introducing a customer to a lender, a consumer hire provider or another credit broker. The required permission depends on what the dealer does and its business model. Receiving no commission does not, by itself, mean an introduction falls outside credit broking.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Follow the introduction, not just the payment",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Identify where the customer goes after asking about finance. A dealer that passes an enquiry to another broker still needs to consider its own regulated role. The CCR009 completion notes give examples of dealer introductions to finance providers and to intermediaries, whether or not a fee is earned."
        ],
        "bullets": [],
        "columns": [
          "Stage",
          "Questions to record"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Customer enquiry",
            "Who explains the service, captures details and provides information?"
          ],
          [
            "Introduction",
            "Is the recipient a lender, hire provider or another broker?"
          ],
          [
            "Agreement",
            "What credit or hire agreement is being considered, and who provides it?"
          ],
          [
            "Payment and remuneration",
            "What fees or commission arise, who pays them and how are they explained?"
          ],
          [
            "Part-exchange",
            "Does anyone help arrange settlement of existing finance?"
          ]
        ],
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "notes",
            "label": "FCA Handbook: SUP 16 Annex 38D — completion notes",
            "href": "https://handbook.fca.org.uk/handbook/sup16/sup16s153"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "id": "guide-section-1"
      },
      {
        "title": "Credit broking is different from lending",
        "paragraphs": [
          "If the dealership introduces a customer to a third-party lender, describe that role accurately. If a business also lends, its lending and broking roles need to be distinguished in the relevant communications.",
          "An introduction is not a lender’s approval. Avoid wording that promises acceptance or implies every customer will receive finance."
        ],
        "bullets": [],
        "columns": [],
        "rows": [],
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "promotions",
            "label": "FCA: key rules for credit brokers",
