      },
      {
        "title": "Build checks around definitions",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Two totals can look plausible while measuring different things. Write the field definition beside the source figure and explain any adjustments. If a number is unexpectedly different from the previous period, investigate the reason rather than changing it simply to make it look consistent.",
          "Use the correct question period or date. A field asking for a snapshot cannot safely be answered with an annual total."
