  "/when-is-ccr009-due": {
    "title": "When Is CCR009 Due? Reporting Periods and Deadlines",
    "answer": "CCR009 uses calendar-based reporting periods, with a 40-business-day submission window. Most firms report annually; some report twice a year. Check the exact period and due date on your firm’s My FCA schedule. The £5 million boundary and first reporting period need care because the FCA’s overview and Handbook wording are not fully aligned.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Reporting frequency and the submission window",
        "paragraphs": [],
        "bullets": [
          "At exactly £5 million, the ongoing Handbook rule uses “£5 million or less” for annual reporting, but the FCA overview uses “£5m or more” for twice-yearly reporting. Note 12(g) and (h) also overlap at that boundary for firms entering scope in January–June from 2026. Ask the FCA to confirm the applicable schedule if this affects your firm; this guide does not resolve that official inconsistency."
        ],
        "columns": [
          "Point",
          "What it means"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Ongoing annual rule",
            "Annual credit-related regulated activity revenue of £5 million or less: 1 January–31 December."
          ],
          [
            "Ongoing twice-yearly rule",
            "Revenue above £5 million: 1 January–30 June and 1 January–31 December. The year-end submission is not just July–December."
          ],
          [
            "First reporting period",
            "Separate first-period provisions apply; check Note 12(f)–(i) and the firm’s schedule."
          ],
          [
            "Submission window",
            "40 business days; do not treat this as 40 calendar days."
          ],
          [
            "Firm-specific deadline",
            "Check the schedule and resolve any mismatch with the FCA rather than guessing."
          ]
